# DESK13 run F -- the delete path, which now goes through the *same*
# `ADCPYDEL` box (title `DELETE FILE(S)`) instead of the NewTOS stand-in alert
# `fun_del` used to raise. Both answers.
# File title x 64..112; `Delete...` is entry 11 of the File box (nine items +
# two separators), y = 19 + 11*16 = 195..211, centre 203.
# Box OK (229,301), Cancel (411,301) as in run C.
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 key 38
1450 key 2e
1500 key ae
1550 key b8
2400 mark B_ALTC
2700 move 431 105
2900 down
2903 up
2910 down
2913 up
3600 parkbr
4300 mark C_SUBDIR
4600 move 287 130
5200 down
5400 up
6000 parkbr
6600 mark D_SELECTED
7000 move 88 8
7600 move 92 203
8200 down
8400 up
9000 parkbr
9800 mark E_DELBOX
10200 move 411 301
10800 down
11000 up
11600 parkbr
12400 mark F_CANCELLED
# After a delete attempt -- cancelled or not -- EmuTOS rebuilds the window
# (`fun_del` -> `fun_rebld`, `deskfun.c:1421-1422`), which re-scans the
# directory and clears `f_selected`. So the file has to be selected again
# before the second attempt; the first cut of this script did not, and
# `File -> Delete...` correctly did nothing.
12800 move 287 130
13400 down
13600 up
14200 parkbr
14800 move 88 8
15400 move 92 203
16000 down
16200 up
16800 parkbr
17600 mark G_DELBOX2
18000 move 229 301
18600 down
18800 up
19400 parkbr
20200 mark H_DELETED
